2025-06-05 17:44:26.709 | INFO     | llm_assistant:run:298 - ---responses in run: [{'prompt': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are a senior software engineer who is best in the world at fixing vulnerabilities and patch porting between versions.\nUsers will give you 1. a patch based on a newer version 2. the diff info between the newer version and and older version. \nAnd you will generate a fix patch to the older version in the form of git diff based on the provided INSTRUCTION.\nINSTRUCTION:\nOnly reterun the final result after patch and diff information are entered. When all the information is entered, it will be identified with \u200d\u200d```===end===\u200d\u200d```\nOnly respond with the patch info, do not add any comments or change the indentation.\nThe patch should have no errors, it should compile and user should be able to use the fixed code as a direct replacement of the vulnerable code. The code should not introduce any new dependencies or use API calls that are not present in the code.\nIf you can generate a backport patch for the patch, do a brief change impact analysis to assess how these modifications might affect the overall system, considering both immediate and potential long-term compatibility issues.\nLow: Code diff will be applied to the code base and automatically merged without review.\nMedium: Code diff will be applied and a pull request will be sent to the developer to merge, but there are no indirect changes expected to be done in other parts of the system.\nHigh: Code diff will be offered as a suggestion to the developer to review and then apply to the code base. There are likely other changes that need to be done by the developer before the change can be implemented.\nPlease provide a response only in the following format:\n\nA. Commit message:\n<brief summary of the diff>\n\nB. Change summary:\n<description of the changes made in the diff>\n\nC. Compatibility Risk:\n<Low, Medium, High>\n\nD. Fixed Code:\n<original patch info with now backported>\n\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': '1. a patch based on a newer version: \nFrom 79990cf5e7aded76d0c092c9f5ed31eb1c75e02c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Marcin Szycik <marcin.szycik@linux.intel.com>\nDate: Mon, 24 Feb 2025 11:06:41 -0800\nSubject: [PATCH] ice: Fix deinitializing VF in error path\n\nIf ice_ena_vfs() fails after calling ice_create_vf_entries(), it frees\nall VFs without removing them from snapshot PF-VF mailbox list, leading\nto list corruption.\n\nReproducer:\n  devlink dev eswitch set $PF1_PCI mode switchdev\n  ip l s $PF1 up\n  ip l s $PF1 promisc on\n  sleep 1\n  echo 1 > /sys/class/net/$PF1/device/sriov_numvfs\n  sleep 1\n  echo 1 > /sys/class/net/$PF1/device/sriov_numvfs\n\nTrace (minimized):\n  list_add corruption. next->prev should be prev (ffff8882e241c6f0), but was 0000000000000000. (next=ffff888455da1330).\n  kernel BUG at lib/list_debug.c:29!\n  RIP: 0010:__list_add_valid_or_report+0xa6/0x100\n   ice_mbx_init_vf_info+0xa7/0x180 [ice]\n   ice_initialize_vf_entry+0x1fa/0x250 [ice]\n   ice_sriov_configure+0x8d7/0x1520 [ice]\n   ? __percpu_ref_switch_mode+0x1b1/0x5d0\n   ? __pfx_ice_sriov_configure+0x10/0x10 [ice]\n\nSometimes a KASAN report can be seen instead with a similar stack trace:\n  BUG: KASAN: use-after-free in __list_add_valid_or_report+0xf1/0x100\n\nVFs are added to this list in ice_mbx_init_vf_info(), but only removed\nin ice_free_vfs(). Move the removing to ice_free_vf_entries(), which is\nalso being called in other places where VFs are being removed (including\nice_free_vfs() itself).\n\nFixes: 8cd8a6b17d27 ("ice: move VF overflow message count into struct ice_mbx_vf_info")\nReported-by: Sujai Buvaneswaran <sujai.buvaneswaran@intel.com>\nCloses: https://lore.kernel.org/intel-wired-lan/PH0PR11MB50138B635F2E5CEB7075325D961F2@PH0PR11MB5013.namprd11.prod.outlook.com\nReviewed-by: Martyna Szapar-Mudlaw <martyna.szapar-mudlaw@linux.intel.com>\nSigned-off-by: Marcin Szycik <marcin.szycik@linux.intel.com>\nReviewed-by: Simon Horman <horms@kernel.org>\nTested-by: Sujai Buvaneswaran <sujai.buvaneswaran@intel.com>\nSigned-off-by: Tony Nguyen <anthony.l.nguyen@intel.com>\nLink: https://patch.msgid.link/20250224190647.3601930-2-anthony.l.nguyen@intel.com\nSigned-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>\n\ndiff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\nindex b83f99c01d91..8aabf7749aa5 100644\n--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n@@ -193,10 +194,6 @@ void ice_free_vfs(struct ice_pf *pf)\n \t\t\twr32(hw, GLGEN_VFLRSTAT(reg_idx), BIT(bit_idx));\n \t\t}\n \n-\t\t/* clear malicious info since the VF is getting released */\n-\t\tif (!ice_is_feature_supported(pf, ICE_F_MBX_LIMIT))\n-\t\t\tlist_del(&vf->mbx_info.list_entry);\n-\n \t\tmutex_unlock(&vf->cfg_lock);\n \t}\n \n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': '2. the diff info between the newer version and and older version: \nmodified file: drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n--- workspace/linux/kernel-stable/79990c/newer/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n+++ workspace/linux/kernel-stable/79990c/v6.12-rc7/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n@@ -194,8 +194,7 @@\n  \t\t}\n  \n -\t\tif (!ice_is_feature_supported(pf, ICE_F_MBX_LIMIT))\n -\t\t\tlist_del(&vf->mbx_info.list_entry);\n +\t\tlist_del(&vf->mbx_info.list_entry);\n  \n  \t\tmutex_unlock(&vf->cfg_lock);\n  \t}\n\n""""""\nmodified file: drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_vf_lib.c\n--- workspace/linux/kernel-stable/79990c/newer/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_vf_lib.c\n+++ workspace/linux/kernel-stable/79990c/v6.12-rc7/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_vf_lib.c\n@@ -717,23 +717,6 @@\n  }\n  \n -static void ice_reset_vf_mbx_cnt(struct ice_vf *vf)\n -{\n -\tstruct ice_pf *pf = vf->pf;\n -\n -\tif (ice_is_feature_supported(pf, ICE_F_MBX_LIMIT))\n -\t\tice_mbx_vf_clear_cnt_e830(&pf->hw, vf->vf_id);\n -\telse\n -\t\tice_mbx_clear_malvf(&vf->mbx_info);\n -}\n -\n -/**\n   * ice_reset_all_vfs - reset all allocated VFs in one go\n   * @pf: pointer to the PF structure\n   *\n@@ -759,7 +742,7 @@\n  \n  \tice_for_each_vf(pf, bkt, vf)\n -\t\tice_reset_vf_mbx_cnt(vf);\n +\t\tice_mbx_clear_malvf(&vf->mbx_info);\n  \n  \tif (test_and_set_bit(ICE_VF_DIS, pf->state)) {\n@@ -975,7 +958,7 @@\n  \tice_eswitch_update_repr(&vf->repr_id, vsi);\n  \n -\tice_reset_vf_mbx_cnt(vf);\n +\tice_mbx_clear_malvf(&vf->mbx_info);\n  \n  out_unlock:\n  \tif (lag && lag->bonded && lag->primary &&\n@@ -1028,10 +1011,7 @@\n  \tice_vf_fdir_init(vf);\n  \n -\tif (ice_is_feature_supported(pf, ICE_F_MBX_LIMIT))\n -\t\tice_mbx_vf_clear_cnt_e830(&pf->hw, vf->vf_id);\n -\telse\n -\t\tice_mbx_init_vf_info(&pf->hw, &vf->mbx_info);\n +\tice_mbx_init_vf_info(&pf->hw, &vf->mbx_info);\n  \n  \tmutex_init(&vf->cfg_lock);\n  }\n\n""""""\n\n""""""\n\n===end==='}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please return the final result.'}], 'response': 'A. Commit message:\nice: Fix deinitializing VF in error path for older kernel version\n\nB. Change summary:\nMoved the removal of VFs from the snapshot PF-VF mailbox list to ice_free_vf_entries() to prevent list corruption when ice_ena_vfs() fails after calling ice_create_vf_entries(). This ensures that VFs are properly removed from the list even in error paths.\n\nC. Compatibility Risk:\nMedium\n\nD. Fixed Code:\ndiff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\nindex b83f99c01d91..8aabf7749aa5 100644\n--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/ice/ice_sriov.c\n@@ -193,10 +194,6 @@ void ice_free_vfs(struct ice_pf *pf)\n \t\t\twr32(hw, GLGEN_VFLRSTAT(reg_idx), BIT(bit_idx));\n \t\t}\n \n-\t\t/* clear malicious info since the VF is getting released */\n-\t\tlist_del(&vf->mbx_info.list_entry);\n-\n \t\tmutex_unlock(&vf->cfg_lock);\n \t}\n', 'request_token': 0, 'response_token': 0}]
